<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ermesinda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Ermesinda of Asturias</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ermesinda was a daughter of Pelagius, founder of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a>. Her marriage to Alfonso, son of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-cantabria">Peter of Cantabria</a>, joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturia">Asturias</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabria">Cantabria</a>, and on the death of her brother Favila in 739 the throne passed to her husband as Alfonso I. She was the mother of King Fruela I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ermesinda.jpg" alt="Ermesinda" width="320" height="514" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joaquín Gutiérrez de la Vega · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ermesinda,_reina_consorte_de_Asturias_(Museo_del_Prado).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
